+### 5.2 Frame-granular validation (`experiments/validation/`)
+One model step is one ADC sample, but one 500 µs RTL step contains about 240 ADC frames (240–241 `sample_valid` pulses per 25000 clocks, measured). To test the granularity explanation directly: (a) each of 9 patterns (1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 20 and 240 invalid frames; 1 and 4 railed frames) was applied one stimulus word per ADC frame to both the RTL and the model, 577 frame-by-frame comparisons of `safe_state`, command, trip bits, sensor-fault and e-stop flags: 0 differences; (b) every original step was expanded into 240 model samples and the model's end-of-step output compared with the existing step-level RTL log: 0 differences in 839 steps. In both RTL and model one invalid frame inhibits for one frame without a latched fault, and the sensor fault latches on the 4th consecutive invalid frame. For (b) the window counter of the model copy used for validation was widened (the original `uint8_t` cannot hold a 1442-frame window); an earlier run before that fix reported 30 spurious predictor mismatches, which were traced to this setup error and are not RTL differences. Both checks regenerate byte-identically from the saved sources (`experiments/validation/run_validation.py`, `step_expansion_check.py`). They compare the RTL with a model written by the same author, and compare only end-of-step (b) or per-frame (a) observations of constant-code stimuli.
+
+### 5.3 Watchdog timing (`experiments/validation/watchdog/`)
+The model's sensor-fault watchdog is 2 missing samples; the RTL's is 2000 clocks (`WD_CYCLES`), i.e. it faults only when the gap between valid samples exceeds 2000 clk, which at 104 clk per frame is 19 or more consecutive missing frames. Frame-granular dropout runs (10 dropout lengths, 1–40 frames) give: RTL faults for ≥19 missing frames and not for ≤18; the shipped model (`WD_STEPS`=2) faults for ≥2 and differs from the RTL for 9–25 frames per run until the operator clear (persistent, not transient); a model with `WD_STEPS`=19 reproduces the RTL's fault/no-fault outcome for every length tested and differs in exactly one transient frame (the 19th missing slot, where the model faults at 1976 clk and the RTL at 2000 clk); `WD_STEPS`=20 misses the 19-frame case. Evidence: `experiments/validation/watchdog/results/watchdog_frame_summary.md`.
 
